WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:03.577
- [Narrator] Covering a
half-acre with hanging flowers,

00:00:03.577 --> 00:00:05.296
the oldest known wisteria in Japan

00:00:05.296 --> 00:00:06.947
is the centerpiece of this brilliantly

00:00:06.947 --> 00:00:09.197
pastel-colored flower park.

00:00:11.326 --> 00:00:13.927
Located in Tochigi, Japan, just over

00:00:13.927 --> 00:00:15.716
an hour train ride from Tokyo,

00:00:15.716 --> 00:00:18.171
is Ashikaga Flower Park.

00:00:18.171 --> 00:00:20.128
The park spans 23 acres and is home

00:00:20.128 --> 00:00:24.448
to more than 350 wisterias
and other flowers.

00:00:24.448 --> 00:00:26.787
The colors vary depending
on the flowering season,

00:00:26.787 --> 00:00:30.620
from pinks and purples,
to yellows and whites.

00:00:31.747 --> 00:00:33.036
Some features of the park include

00:00:33.036 --> 00:00:35.456
the wisteria tunnel and floating gardens,

00:00:35.456 --> 00:00:38.211
but the pride and joy
of Ashikaga Flower Park

00:00:38.211 --> 00:00:41.158
is the Great Miracle Wisteria.

00:00:41.158 --> 00:00:43.608
The 140-year-old sprawling tree

00:00:43.608 --> 00:00:45.738
is located in a place of pride,

00:00:45.738 --> 00:00:47.976
right in the center of the park.

00:00:47.976 --> 00:00:49.861
After nightfall, the site is lit up

00:00:49.861 --> 00:00:53.907
so these draping flowers
can be seen at all hours.

00:00:53.907 --> 00:00:55.637
The vivid yellow wisteria begins blooming

00:00:55.637 --> 00:00:58.197
at the start of May and is the only one

00:00:58.197 --> 00:00:59.947
of its kind in Japan.

00:01:00.927 --> 00:01:02.176
The park is a year-round attraction

00:01:02.176 --> 00:01:03.888
with seasonal plants that creates

00:01:03.888 --> 00:01:06.437
an ever-changing sense of magnificence

00:01:06.437 --> 00:01:08.326
as nature puts on a show.

00:01:08.326 --> 00:01:12.409
(casual upbeat background music)

